---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects personal data, including cookies, analytics, advertising (Google AdSense) and your rights.`}
  updated={SITE.legalUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information {SITE.name} ("we", "us") collects when you visit <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong>,
    how we use it, and the choices you have. We keep data collection to the minimum needed to run the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} is operated by {SITE.author.name}, India. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <h3>Reading the site</h3>
  <p>
    You can read every article without an account. Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes your IP address and
    request headers to deliver pages and to block attacks; Cloudflare keeps standard server logs for a limited time.
  </p>
  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies and does not track you across sites. It gives us
    aggregate numbers such as page views and country. We may also use Google Analytics in future; if we do, this policy
    will be updated and consent will be requested where the law requires it.
  </p>
  <h3>Contact form</h3>
  <p>
    When you use the contact form we receive the name, email address and message you type, plus your IP address for
    abuse prevention. The message is delivered by our email provider (Resend) to our inbox and kept only as long as
    needed to reply and keep a record of the conversation.
  </p>
  <h3>Accounts for community writers and commenters</h3>
  <p>
    If you sign in with Google to write or comment, we receive your Google account's name, email address and profile
    picture, and we store them with the content you publish. We do not receive your Google password. You can delete
    your account at any time from your profile page; published articles can be deleted with it or kept under an
    anonymised byline, at your choice.
  </p>
  <h3>Content moderation</h3>
  <p>
    Community submissions are checked automatically for spam and harmful content before publication. The text and
    images you submit may be sent to automated moderation services (OpenAI's moderation API and Cloudflare Workers AI)
    for that purpose only. We keep a log of moderation decisions to review and improve them.
  </p>
  <h3>Bot protection</h3>
  <p>
    Forms are protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, which analyses browser signals to tell people from bots. Turnstile does
    not show tracking ads and does not build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>We intend to display advertising served by Google AdSense. The following disclosures apply once ads are shown:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or
      other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this
      site and/or other sites on the Internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also
      opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalised advertising at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Other third-party ad networks, if any, may also use cookies; their privacy policies govern that use. We will list
      them here.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Visitors from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are shown a consent message before any
    personalised advertising cookies are set, and can change their choice at any time through the "Privacy settings"
    link in the footer (shown in those regions).
  </p>
  <p>
    Cookies we set ourselves: a session cookie when you sign in, and a preference cookie if you choose settings such as
    a theme. We do not set cookies for visitors who only read.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis and retention</h2>
  <p>
    We process data to provide the site (contract and legitimate interest), to keep it secure (legitimate interest), and
    for advertising with your consent where required. Server and moderation logs are kept for up to 90 days, contact
    messages for up to 2 years, and account data until you delete your account.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal data. We share it only with the service providers named above (Cloudflare, Google, Resend,
    OpenAI, Sentry for error reports), each bound by its own privacy terms, and when the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what data we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or object to its processing.
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. We answer within 30 days. Residents of
    India have rights under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023; residents of the EEA and UK under the GDPR;
    residents of California under the CCPA.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The site is not directed at children under 13 (under 16 in the EEA). We do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We will post any changes on this page and update the date at the top. Significant changes will be announced on the home page.</p>
</PageLayout>
